From: avlo-py-build <py-build@avlo.local>
Subject: [PATCH] AVLO: fork API types — declare _module/_api + Module runtime exports for d.ts emission

Type-only, zero runtime bytes (declare/interface edits only — the built
glue + wasm stay byte-identical, so this patch alone rotates nothing):
- api.ts: `declare static _module` / `_api` on PyodideAPI_ so the emitted
  pyodide.d.ts types the fork-private surfaces the app boots, captures
  and restores through (makePublicAPI has assigned them untyped since
  upstream; the d.ts silently dropped them).
- types.ts: PyodideModule gains the runtime-export members the app uses
  (wasmTable / growMemory / callMain — all real at runtime via 0001's
  EXPORTED_RUNTIME_METHODS; upstream never declared them; exitCode was
  already on EmscriptenModule).
  Only the app-used surface is declared — extend as consumers appear.
- pyodide.ts: _avloRestore.preBlit params typed (PyodideModule +
  PyodideModule["API"]) and the return widened with `undefined` (a cold
  main returns undefined — finalizeBootstrap(undefined) IS the cold
  branch; the old annotation predated that contract).
Consumer: stage.mjs stages dist/raw/pyodide.d.ts as
web/src/core/py/pyodide-fork.gen.d.ts (checked in, drift-gated, never
hashed into buildHash — types carry no runtime bytes).

